<title>RUSSIA: Rouble edges down as speculators shun thin market.</title>
<headline>Rouble edges down as speculators shun thin market.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1996-12-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The rouble edged down on Thursday in thin trade as a few banks filled client orders ahead of the end of the year, but speculative traders stayed out of the market, dealers said.</p>
<p> roubles/dollar	 Dec 26 midday  Dec 26 early  Dec 25 close</p>
<p> today settlement     5,559-61	 5,557-58	-</p>
<p> tomorrow settlement  5,561-62	 5,558-61	5,558-59</p>
<p> overnight credit (%) 15-25	    20-25	   20-30</p>
<p>			    Dec 26			     Dec 25</p>
<p> central bank	   5,548/62			   5,548/62</p>
<p> MICEX		    5,550				5,550</p>
<p>Interbank Finance House chief dealer Mikhail Kulinich said trade would likely remain thin through the Russian Orthodox Christmas on January 7.</p>
<p>&quot;Nothing special is going on, just client orders,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>&quot;Speculative trading is not attractive now as the market is too thin.&quot;</p>
<p>--Artyom Danielyan, Moscow newsroom (095) 941 8520</p>
